Q: Why does my custom hook cause an infinite re-render in React even though dependencies seem correct? A: <p>Because fetch data is a new function on every render and when the effect run it sets state and make effect run again hence end up with infinite loop. So either move your fetch data code inside useeffect like below :-</p>
<pre><code>useEffect(() =&gt; {
    const fetchData = async () =&gt; {
    const response = await fetch(url);
    const json = await response.json();
    setData(json);
  };
   fetchData();
}, [url]);
</code></pre>
<p>Or as mentioned in the comments memoize the fetch data function using callback like below:-</p>
<pre><code>const fetchData = useCallback(async () =&gt; {
    const response = await fetch(url);
    const json = await response.json();
    setData(json);
  },[url]);


</code></pre>
